Kernel_isValidSignature
├── when hash equals ERC7739_MAGIC_HASH
│   └── it should return ERC7739 support indicator
└── when hash is not ERC7739_MAGIC_HASH
    ├── given the structured signature is truncated
    │   └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    ├── given the signature includes the removed validation-mode prefix
    │   └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    ├── given the validation type is ROOT
    │   ├── given the signature format is TypedDataSign
    │   │   ├── when the root validator returns valid
    │   │   │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
    │   │   └── when the root validator returns invalid
    │   │       └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    │   ├── given the signature format is PersonalSign
    │   │   ├── it should wrap the hash with PersonalSign struct
    │   │   ├── when the root validator returns valid
    │   │   │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
    │   │   └── when the root validator returns invalid
    │   │       └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    │   └── given the signature includes domain separator and contents
    │       └── it should verify the full TypedDataSign structure
    ├── given the validation type is VALIDATOR
    │   ├── given the signature format is TypedDataSign
    │   │   ├── when the validator returns valid
    │   │   │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
    │   │   └── when the validator returns invalid
    │   │       └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    │   └── given the signature format is PersonalSign
    │       ├── when the validator returns valid
    │       │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
    │       └── when the validator returns invalid
    │           └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    ├── given the validation type is PERMISSION
    │   ├── given the signature format is TypedDataSign
    │   │   ├── when all policies pass and signer returns valid
    │   │   │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
    │   │   ├── when any policy fails
    │   │   │   └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    │   │   └── when signer returns invalid
    │   │       └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    │   └── given the signature format is PersonalSign
    │       ├── when all policies pass and signer returns valid
    │       │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
    │       └── when any policy or signer fails
    │           └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    ├── given the validation type is unsupported
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidValidationType error
    ├── given the signature is wrapped with ERC6492 sentinel
    │   └── it should unwrap and validate the inner signature
    ├── given the signature format is TypedDataSign with explicit contentsName
    │   ├── when the root validator returns valid
    │   │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
    │   └── when the root validator returns invalid
    │       └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    ├── given the signature format is replayable TypedDataSign with explicit contentsName
    │   ├── when the root validator returns valid
    │   │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
    │   └── when the root validator returns invalid
    │       └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
    ├── given the root validation is not set
    │   └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID via base fallback signature
    └── given the signature format is replayable TypedDataSign
        ├── when the root validator returns valid for replayable
        │   └── it should return ERC1271_MAGICVALUE
        └── when the root validator returns invalid for replayable
            └── it should return ERC1271_INVALID
